  "body_human_readable": "![Oklahoma City Thunder logo](https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5d/Oklahoma_City_Thunder.svg/1200px-Oklahoma_City_Thunder.svg.png)\n\n### Oklahoma City Thunder Clinch 2025 NBA Title\n\nThe Oklahoma City Thunder won the 2025 NBA Finals, defeating the Indiana Pacers in a thrilling seven-game series. The victory marks the franchise's first championship since relocating to Oklahoma City in 2008 and their second title in franchise history, the first being in 1979 as the Seattle SuperSonics.\n\nThe Thunder secured the championship with a 103-91 victory in the decisive Game 7, held at their home court, the Paycom Center. The series, which concluded on June 22, 2025, was the first NBA Finals to go to a Game 7 since 2016.\n\n**Shai Gilgeous-Alexander Named Finals MVP**\n\nFresh off of winning the regular-season MVP award, Thunder superstar Shai Gilgeous-Alexander was named the Bill Russell NBA Finals Most Valuable Player. He received all 11 media votes for the award. Gilgeous-Alexander delivered a standout performance throughout the series, averaging 30.3 points, 5.6 assists, and 4.6 rebounds per game. In the final game, he led the Thunder with 29 points and 12 assists. This achievement made him the first player since 2000 to win the league's scoring title, the regular-season MVP, and the Finals MVP in the same season.\n\n**Path to the Championship**\n\nThe Thunder entered the finals as the Western Conference champions after a dominant season where they finished with a league-best 68-14 record. The Indiana Pacers, champions of the Eastern Conference, fought valiantly throughout the series. The Pacers' efforts in Game 7 were hampered by a significant injury to star player Tyrese Haliburton, who tore his right Achilles tendon in the first quarter.\n\nThe Thunder's victory capped a historic season, tying the 1996-97 Chicago Bulls for the third-most total wins in a season with 84 (including playoffs). The 2025 Finals also marked the seventh consecutive year with a different NBA champion, the longest such streak in league history.",
